<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gesta Hungarorum</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1200</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gesta Hungarorum is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> chronicle of the Hungarian conquest of the Carpathian Basin, written around 1200 by an anonymous notary of a King Béla. It describes local rulers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glad">Glad</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menumorut">Menumorut</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelou">Gelou</a> resisting the Hungarians around 900. Because these figures appear in no other source, its reliability is much debated.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum.jpg" alt="Gesta Hungarorum" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gesta_Hungarorum_Anonymous.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
